WEBVTT

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.970
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:12.070
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:17.650
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:26.420
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:34.160
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:36.630
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:39.500
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:44.240
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.900
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:54.580
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.580 --> 00:01:01.250
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.630
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:12.270
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:17.170
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:22.410
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:32.520
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:37.260
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:41.990
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:50.900
Yes?

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:53.600
<i>Hello, Madoka-san!</i>

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.840
-Oh, hello! Just a sec.
-Sure!

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.940
Ayumu! You have a visitor!

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:02.610
Who?

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:05.150
That girl with the weird song...

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:06.910
Tell her I'm not home.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.290
Sorry to intrude!

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:13.390
What's her problem, today's a day off...

00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:14.720
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:16.160
What kind of attitude is that?!

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.190
Someone gave up their day off
for you, you know!

00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:21.700
What do you want?

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:23.630
Don't give me that!

00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:26.700
Let's take time out to review
all of the incidents so far

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:30.170
and find a clue to solving
all the mysteries!

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:34.280
Do it by yourself.
You don't need me for that.

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:35.800
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:39.250
Okay, okay!

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:42.620
Alright, Ayumu. I'm leaving now.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:43.650
Okay.

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:46.920
Oh, you're leaving?

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:50.360
I have a bit of work.
Make yourself at home.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.190
I will! Bye!

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:54.560
See you later!

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:59.570
<i>Madoka-san is so wonderful...</i>

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:01.000
You think?

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.770
All she does is work, and she
can't do anything woman-like.

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:06.880
You sound old-fashioned!

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:10.710
We're entering an era when women
hold their own in society, you know!

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:13.820
<i>I want to be just like
Madoka-san when I grow older!</i>

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:15.250
Do whatever you want...

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.240
Eww! Dog poo!

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:21.590
<i>...just don't try too hard
to be like her.</i>

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:25.230
Never mind, let's get started.

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:26.520
Right...

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:31.230
<i>It all began when your
older brother, Kiyotaka-san,</i>

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.290
disappeared two years ago...

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:37.240
"I'm going to pursue the
mystery of the Blade Children...

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:40.240
Until I attain the unseen
truth with these two hands...

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:42.540
Tell Madoka for me too."

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:47.450
<i>After he left that mysterious message,
Kiyotaka-san simply disappeared.</i>

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:52.450
Afterward, you entered
Tsukiomi Academy.

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:55.660
And then the first incident occurred...

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:58.590
The attempted murder
of Sayoko Shiranagatani...

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.670
Are you alright?!

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:09.600
Say something!

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.170
What's going on?

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:14.440
Talk about dangerous,
there's no fence here!

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:17.310
Did you do this? Did you push her off?!

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:22.220
Huh?

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:24.220
And since all the suspicion was on you,

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:26.020
you searched for the real culprit.

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:28.090
Using your unrivaled power of deduction,

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:30.690
you discovered the truth
behind the incident...

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:34.490
Well, you did support me too...

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:44.640
The melody of logic
always plays the truth.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:46.900
<i>Sonobe-sensei. The one who did this...</i>

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:53.720
...was you!

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:58.790
<i>But right after that,
Sonobe-sensei was attacked too...</i>

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:03.220
All the incidents revolve
around the Blade Children...

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:07.200
Sayoko Shiranagatani was one of them.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.600
Afterwards, the Blade Children caused

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:12.670
one terrifying incident after another.

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:16.130
Kosuke Asazuki and Rio Takeuchi...

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:27.080
You don't mean...
you killed Sonobe?!

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:34.920
He's been shadowing us
for a long time now.

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:37.090
He wanted to kill us all.

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:39.030
You don't mean that you're...

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:43.100
My name is Kosuke Asazuki.

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:46.000
Yes, I am one of the Blade Children.

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:51.970
Do you intend to oppose us,
no matter what?

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:53.110
You're...

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:56.310
One of the Blade Children...
Rio Takeuchi.

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:58.980
Even a girl like you, too?!

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:03.550
<i>Could you refrain from telling
Ayumu Narumi-san about us?</i>

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:05.990
Don't you think that's a little unfair?

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:09.390
Do you actually believe fate is fair?

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:10.430
If it is,

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:14.190
then I wonder if the Blade Children
would have been born at all...

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:19.130
I've decided to switch sides
and hunt you instead...

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:21.140
If you're insistent
on getting in our way,

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:23.070
then there's no other choice.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.370
<i>Imazato-sensei.</i>

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:35.480
Goodbye.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.550
<i>By the way, Narumi-san...</i>

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:41.960
What?

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:44.620
I'm a little thirsty...

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:48.300
Here.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:49.960
Wow, cocoa!

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:53.330
Hot cocoa is perfect on cold days!

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:57.640
<i>Delicious! You amaze me, Narumi-san!</i>

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:59.370
This cocoa tastes like
happiness that you've brought

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:02.780
from a far-off, springtime country...

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:05.480
It makes me want to sing...

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:10.720
Outside the window, kira kira kira ri

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:14.320
A shooting star streaks

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:16.060
Just continue.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:16.790
Right.

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:19.730
And then the life-or-death battle

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:22.600
<i>between you and
Rio Takeuchi-san began...</i>

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:24.930
Can we help you?

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:28.600
Well, I found this in a
hallway on the first floor.

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:32.140
This was taped to the kitty's head...

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:33.570
"Take me to the Newspaper Office"

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:35.840
Don't tell me there's
a bomb inside it?!

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:37.110
Hey, now!

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:59.260
I won't let you get away,
Blade Child!

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:04.040
<i>Well played, younger brother
of Kiyotaka-sama.</i>

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:07.440
I'm impressed you could tell
I was one of the Blade Children!

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:13.880
But if we keep matching
our wits like this,

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:16.920
I don't think we'll
ever reach a conclusion...

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:18.110
<i>Kosuke-kun!</i>

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:22.320
This is one messed-up situation.

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:24.990
You sure you can do this?

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:28.000
Don't worry. I had an inkling
it would come to this.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:33.090
Now then, Little Brother, let us
begin our non-rigged last game...

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:37.700
Both cups contain sugar water!

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:47.520
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:48.820
<i>Impossible!</i>

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:51.120
<i>This tongue-piercing bitterness...</i>

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:52.520
<i>Strychnine!</i>

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:54.290
Just what I'd expect from you.

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:55.860
Even though you talked big,

00:08:55.860 --> 00:09:00.090
you could barely raise the cup to your
lips without being extra cautious.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:02.760
There's not nearly enough
in there for a lethal dose.

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:05.820
You can't change your fate like that.

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:13.240
I told you it wasn't rigged...

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:16.730
<i>She really did bet her life on this!</i>

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:22.450
<i>I killed Imazato-sensei easily, too.</i>

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:26.250
-And before you knew it, you were
deeply involved in the incidents
-I've been waiting for you to say that!

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:29.690
-As you pursued the mystery
of the Blade Children
-I just recorded everything you've said!

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:31.960
That your brother spoke of.

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:35.800
"Dragged into them"
would be more precise.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:39.130
<i>-The secret behind who
the Blade Children are
-Narumi-san!</i>

00:09:39.130 --> 00:09:42.340
And why they cause one
incident after another...

00:09:42.340 --> 00:09:44.740
-And the identities of the "Hunters"
-Hand it over, unless you wanna
see this girl fall from here.

00:09:44.740 --> 00:09:46.770
<i>-Who target them...
-Narumi-san! Face off
against them one more time!</i>

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:49.440
-But the biggest mystery
-Believe in your strength!

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:54.710
Is why they attach
such importance to you...

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.310
<i>By the way, Narumi-san.</i>

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:01.960
What?

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:04.120
I'm hungry.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.830
What would you like?

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:13.030
Curry!

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:14.590
Curry, huh...

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:19.810
I'm so bored...

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:23.640
I can't believe it's a day off
but I can't go anywhere...

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:26.750
<i>But I'm here, aren't I?</i>

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:29.120
That doesn't make me
a single bit happier.

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:30.820
What're you so pissy about?!

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:35.020
I don't like guys who come into
a girl's room without any presents

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:37.490
and then lounge around
like they own the place...

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:38.930
Well, excuse me...

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:42.260
<i>I bet Eyes-kun would bring me
a present, though...</i>

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:43.930
A net-patterned one!

00:10:43.930 --> 00:10:45.430
<i>Melon again?</i>

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:48.440
There's no way I could buy
you anything that expensive...

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:51.000
You're such a big cheapskate! Leave!

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:56.740
Geez, I can't believe
you're the same person

00:10:56.740 --> 00:11:01.650
who risked her life in that
battle with Little Narumi...

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:05.750
Will you accept this match?

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:08.380
Or will you run away?

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:12.590
Fine.

00:11:12.590 --> 00:11:16.960
But I'm sure you'll regret
acting so tough now!

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:21.470
Just try and make me.

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:27.980
The game is to see who can
get both you and the tape,

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:30.810
which will be in a
different part of town.

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:33.510
What's this key for?

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:36.920
It disarms a bomb that's been
set in a certain location.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:39.420
Where is this certain location?

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:41.760
Little Narumi's neck.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:46.560
It's small, but powerful enough
to blow your head off.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:03.780
Let the game begin.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:05.910
Keep away from them
until I get the tape.

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:09.850
If you're near Shumari Station,
then head there and get on a train.

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:11.550
A train?

00:12:11.550 --> 00:12:14.580
You'll be safest
while on a moving train.

00:12:16.020 --> 00:12:18.790
I can tell nearly
everything he's thinking.

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:19.690
Listen.

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:23.860
He'll put himself at risk and wait
until the last half to get the key.

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:26.030
The tape will be his priority for now.

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:26.770
Got it.

00:12:26.770 --> 00:12:29.630
Rush straight for the tape, Kosuke-kun.

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:43.740
Oh no!

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:47.520
Bye bye!

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:50.490
<i>I'm so sorry, Narumi-san!</i>

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:53.650
<i>Rio-san pushed me into a random train!</i>

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:59.090
<i>Sorry, Little Narumi. The tape is...</i>

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:04.340
What the?!

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:07.010
Yeah, sorry 'bout that!

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:11.880
I sent a bunch of dummies to confuse you.

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:13.510
Pretty sweet, huh?

00:13:14.380 --> 00:13:16.050
<i>What the hell?</i>

00:13:16.050 --> 00:13:18.810
<i>Talk about a real blockhead...</i>

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:23.390
You should never let
your guard down. Y'know?

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:30.230
You're looking for this, I take it?

00:13:30.230 --> 00:13:33.370
So you brought it? Thanks a bunch.

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:35.500
I absolutely will not press it for you.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.310
You're going to die.

00:13:37.310 --> 00:13:41.830
No, I absolutely will not die.

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:48.050
Kerosene. I'll burn
pretty good if I explode.

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:49.980
As will this...

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:54.720
You won't be satisfied if you don't
get both my head and the tape.

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:58.210
Unless you press that disarm button,
you will die.

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:00.360
You're right.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:03.330
<i>Assuming it is filled with kerosene.</i>

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:05.900
I replaced it with water.

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:07.460
All that you're going to get...

00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:10.870
...is death.

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:12.470
You can have it if you want.

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:13.940
It's a dummy.

00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:16.480
The real one's still in my mailbox.

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:20.820
All I did was show Asazuki
a pre-prepared package.

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:24.720
You guys misunderstood and
thought I recovered the real one.

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:30.020
Let us welcome the
moment of truth together.

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:32.090
Seven seconds. Six...

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:35.500
Five...Four...Three...

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:36.830
Two...

00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:38.270
One!

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:39.460
Zero!

00:14:47.810 --> 00:14:49.440
No way...

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:51.410
What dumb luck!

00:14:52.710 --> 00:14:54.240
Stay back!

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:57.790
<i>I thought so!</i>

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:01.220
You kept talking to me with
your excessive confidence

00:15:01.220 --> 00:15:05.130
to confuse me and
numb my sense of time...

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:07.060
Impressive.

00:15:07.060 --> 00:15:10.830
<i>You truly are worthy of being
Kiyotaka-sama's younger brother.</i>

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:13.170
But I win!

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:15.970
I saw through you and won!

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:21.580
I guess I can only pray now...

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:27.150
I beseech you, O' Lord!
Save this pitiful sinner!

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:29.550
There's no such thing as God.

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:31.920
Are you so sure?

00:15:33.590 --> 00:15:35.360
Look...

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:37.620
My goddess has arrived!

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:44.800
My prayer has been heard!

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:46.270
<i>Narumi-san!</i>

00:15:53.770 --> 00:15:55.070
Hallelujah!

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:02.450
Even though you lost,
you fought really well

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:05.720
for someone with
life-threatening injuries...

00:16:06.320 --> 00:16:09.260
You're really something.

00:16:09.260 --> 00:16:12.390
<i>At that time, he...</i>

00:16:12.390 --> 00:16:14.600
In terms of actual skill, I lost.

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:16.560
I was just lucky.

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:18.470
That's not true...

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:21.000
I know myself well enough to know.

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:24.470
I always run around
doing things randomly,

00:16:24.470 --> 00:16:27.340
never thinking about the consequences.

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:30.210
<i>Only after I've done things
do I think hard</i>

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:32.740
and make sense out of them.

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:37.820
It's not luck.

00:16:37.820 --> 00:16:41.720
It was your skill that confused me!

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:48.490
My brother wouldn't tremble like me...

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:55.970
<i>If anyone can go where
Kiyotaka-sama couldn't, it's him...</i>

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:59.960
<i>Our fate may change after all!</i>

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:11.990
Rutherford!

00:17:11.990 --> 00:17:13.820
<i>Eyes-kun!</i>

00:17:13.820 --> 00:17:18.950
I was in the neighborhood,
so I stopped by...

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:21.260
You didn't!

00:17:21.260 --> 00:17:24.130
You really did bring me
a net-patterned...

00:17:26.530 --> 00:17:28.370
I have dried fish if you want some.

00:17:28.370 --> 00:17:29.800
-Why?
-Why?

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:35.840
Eyes Rutherford...

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:39.410
I had no idea he was one
of the Blade Children too...

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:43.210
Come to think of it,
when he suddenly called for you...

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:48.640
Somebody bring me the
younger Narumi brother.

00:17:53.730 --> 00:17:55.500
Play.

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:57.460
What?

00:17:57.460 --> 00:18:00.000
Let me hear you play the piano.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.970
I wish to hear how well the
Narumi name actually measures up

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:05.740
to the myths about you
in the piano world.

00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:08.580
Sorry. I gave up the
piano a long time ago.

00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:10.640
What are you so afraid of?

00:18:10.640 --> 00:18:14.310
Is recognizing that you're no comparison
to your brother that frightening?

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:17.950
You've been blessed with a gift...

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:21.190
But you, yourself, know

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:24.490
that your skills are at best
an imitation of your brother's.

00:18:24.490 --> 00:18:28.000
You don't even begin
to compare to the original.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:30.000
Ayumu Narumi.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.520
You will forever be a loser.

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:44.980
I can't believe you're
eating dried fish...

00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:46.310
Are you a cat?

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:47.410
Shut up, meow!

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:48.980
<i>You're so dumb, Kosuke-kun!</i>

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:52.780
I get it! Those are dried,
net-patterned fish!

00:18:55.190 --> 00:18:56.590
<i>Kanone...</i>

00:18:58.730 --> 00:19:01.360
"Eyes, you're too nice.

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:03.230
<i>So you should cry.</i>

00:19:03.230 --> 00:19:05.800
Even if you are one
of the Blade Children.

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:08.900
You don't want to lose
something important to you..."

00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:11.410
"Massacre is our destiny.

00:19:11.410 --> 00:19:16.370
We Blade Children are children
who must not live."

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:21.810
<i>Don't be caught by the darkness,
Kanone...</i>

00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:26.050
<i>The darkness of your own heart...</i>

00:19:29.990 --> 00:19:31.930
Thanks for the food!

00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:34.330
It was delicious!

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:36.360
You know, five bowls
is a little too much...

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:40.200
<i>You're still not going to eat,
Narumi-san?</i>

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:44.030
No, we always eat dinner late.

00:19:47.840 --> 00:19:51.040
Look how late it is! I should go!

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:54.620
Want me to walk you there?

00:19:54.620 --> 00:19:56.180
No, that's okay!

00:19:56.180 --> 00:19:58.990
<i>Well, see you at school tomorrow,
Narumi-san!</i>

00:19:58.990 --> 00:20:01.960
-Yeah. Take care.
-I will!

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:09.690
-He really pisses me off.
-Sorry.

00:20:09.690 --> 00:20:12.790
-Not you.
-Then who?

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:15.860
The old man.

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:19.170
No! Our senior superintendent!

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:20.900
Oh, I see...

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:24.240
What do you mean, "Oh, I see..."?!

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:27.170
Lately he's been coming up
with stupid reasons

00:20:27.170 --> 00:20:29.730
to start arguments with me...

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:36.350
If he doesn't like me,
he should just tell me to my face...

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:39.120
Are you making fun of me?

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:42.120
I'm asking if you're making
fun of me with that attitude!

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:44.560
No, no!

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:48.060
Sorry, I think I'm going to be home
a little later than usual...

00:20:48.060 --> 00:20:49.720
Here you are, one vinegar cucumber!

00:20:59.410 --> 00:21:03.310
"Like a Sweet Aroma Haze"

00:21:05.170 --> 00:21:10.870
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:17.570
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:29.690 --> 00:21:35.730
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:35.730 --> 00:21:41.370
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:41.370 --> 00:21:47.280
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:53.850
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:53.850 --> 00:21:59.590
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:21:59.590 --> 00:22:04.790
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:10.630
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:10.630 --> 00:22:22.240
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:28.020
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:28.020 --> 00:22:34.320
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:38.450 --> 00:22:42.720
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:42.720 --> 00:22:45.390
If you know the enemy and know yourself,

00:22:45.390 --> 00:22:48.660
you needn't fear the result
of a hundred battles!

00:22:48.660 --> 00:22:51.290
<i>Next episode's highlight is
when Narumi-san and Hiyono-chan</i>

00:22:51.290 --> 00:22:53.290
take a romantic walk while eating.

00:22:53.290 --> 00:22:56.130
Sweets don't fill you up!

00:22:56.130 --> 00:22:58.500
On the next Spiral: Bond of Reasoning...

00:22:58.500 --> 00:23:00.000
Like a Swan

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:02.900
Don't look at only your finger
as you point to the moon!

00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:04.310
Does that make sense?

00:23:04.310 --> 00:23:06.870
That's all for today's
Hiyono's Playhouse!
